cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >
  If you use this software in your research, please cite it using the
  metadata below.

title: >
  PAD/OLER SSI Validation: External Validation of a Surgical Site Infection
  Risk Score in Peripheral Arterial Disease Using OMOP CDM

authors:
  - given-names: Adam P.
    family-names: Johnson
    name-suffix: MD MPH
    email: apj20@uke.edu
    affiliation: >-
      Duke University School of Medicine, Department of Surgery,
      Division of Vascular and Endovascular Surgery and
      Department of Population Health Sciences
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-3014-6372"

version: "1.0.0"
date-released: "2026-04-05"

repository-code: "https://github.com/adam-mdmph/pad-oler-ssi-val"
url: "https://github.com/adam-mdmph/pad-oler-ssi-val"

license: GPL-3.0

abstract: >
  An end-to-end external validation pipeline for an integer risk score predicting
  surgical site infection (SSI) following open revascularization for peripheral
  arterial disease (PAD). The pipeline runs on OMOP CDM v5.4 data (SQL Server),
  uses OHDSI PatientLevelPrediction for cohort generation and model evaluation,
  and includes synthetic data generation via a custom Synthea module to support
  reproducible development and testing. Workflow steps cover environment setup,
  cohort definition, Synthea-based synthetic data generation, ETL to OMOP,
  data quality assessment (ACHILLES, OHDSI Data Quality Dashboard), risk score
  evaluation, and manuscript-format report generation.

keywords:
  - peripheral arterial disease
  - surgical site infection
  - external validation
  - prediction model
  - OMOP CDM
  - OHDSI
  - PatientLevelPrediction
  - Synthea
  - real-world data
  - clinical informatics
  - R

